//! Code-to-CID tables for the Adobe-Japan1 predefined CMaps.
//!
//! ISO 32000-1 §9.7.5.2 and Table 118 name the CMaps a Type 0 font may cite
//! as its `/Encoding` instead of embedding a CMap stream. Such a CMap maps a
//! character code to a CID, and the CIDFont's `/W` array is keyed by that CID
//! (§9.7.4.3). Without the table the code itself was used as the key, which
//! is only right for Identity-H/V: under `UniJIS-UCS2-H` or `90ms-RKSJ-H` no
//! `/W` entry matched and every glyph took `/DW`, so proportional and
//! half-width text was laid out at the full-width advance.
//!
//! GENERATED by pdf_dioxide's `tools/gen_predefined_cmaps.py` from the CMap
//! resources Adobe publishes at
//! <https://github.com/adobe-type-tools/cmap-resources> (Adobe-Japan1-7).
//! Do not edit by hand.
//!
//! Only codes of one or two bytes are present (the code iterator yields
//! 16-bit codes). A `-V` CMap holds the codes it changes and reads the rest
//! through its base, as the source file does with `usecmap`.
//!
//! The source files carry this notice:
